<article class="env-lemma" id="0865">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0865">Lemma <span data-tag="0865">71.18.4</span>.</a> In the situation of Definition <a href="/tag/0862" data-tag="0862">71.18.1</a>. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $X$ is flat over $B$ at all points lying over $Z$, then the strict transform of $X$ is equal to the base change $X \times _ B B'$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. If $\mathcal{F}$ is flat over $B$ at all points lying over $Z$, then the strict transform $\mathcal{F}'$ of $\mathcal{F}$ is equal to the pullback $\text{pr}_ X^*\mathcal{F}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: Follows from the case of schemes (Divisors, Lemma <a href="/tag/080F" data-tag="080F">31.34.3</a>) by étale localization (Lemma <a href="/tag/0863" data-tag="0863">71.18.2</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>